  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 1,000eb (Very Expensive)</p>\n<p><em>A classic implant, and one of the more popular Berserk OS’s made by Moore Technologies. Tested and proven in high-stakes combat.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Berserk Operating System.</strong> Berserk can now be activated as half of a ROF 2 Action, and its duration is reduced to 30 seconds (10 Rounds). Non-FBC users without a Cyberspine now suffer a -4 penalty to all Ranged Attacks while Berserk is active.</p>\n<p>While Berserk is active, the first damage the user takes in a Round is reduced by an amount equivalent to half of their BODY, any penalties to STATs or Actions from non-dismemberment Critical Injuries are halved, and the user does not re-suffer any Critical Injury’s bonus damage when moving further than 4m/yds on foot in a Round.</p>\n<p><strong>Enhances:</strong> Berserk<br>\n<strong>Option Slots:</strong> 0 (Cyberware Enhancement)</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Every Operating System is incompatible with every other Operating System and with the base cyberware it is for: none of them can be installed while another OS, or that OS's own base cyberware, is anywhere in the user's body or in a worn apparatus they're connected to. The sheet doesn't enforce that.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Operating Systems &gt; Berserk Operating Systems).</em></p>"
  },
